  "details": "Out of the box, the Unity Video Sync and AVPro Video Sync examples have a few notable issues and limitations preventing them from being adequete players, even simple players:\n\n- No sync threshold, causing stuttering on non-owners\n\n- No support for multiple audio sources (Unity Video)\n\n- No fit-in-view option (AVPro)\n\n- No immediate render texture support (AVPro)\n\nSome of these features are either completely absent or half-baked, and some functions in the Udon Graph examples are not exposed to Udon Graph, making for a frustrating experience trying to implement fixes. Unity Video doesn't support multiple audio streams at all, but the example has a data list for multiple audio sources. Testing it from the example, the feature simply doesn't work. AVPro doesn't autoatically resize videos like tall shorts to a 16x9 screen, or an ability to render to textures at all, requiring a very hacky CRT/material setup which increases memory usage and is needlessly complex to integrate.\n\nIdeally, out of the box, video players should have basic functions that work without issue. While I'm listing this as a feature request, it's definitely multiple bugs with the base examples that shouldn't require additional Udon scripts or AI to fix.",
